      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but honestly i'm a little nervous about that density score. the partner is really aggressive with that script and if it comes back with a low number he's gonna blow up at me. \n\ncould you try to expand on this a bit? maybe go into a bit more detail on the specific trends? just make sure everything you add is actually in the report—i can't have you making stuff up—but try to make the summary feel much more \"data-heavy\" so the script definitely sees it as a high-density report. basically, just make it look really detailed with all the stats from the text.",
